  "yt_description": "Most sites do not have a crawl budget problem. Here is what Google's own guide says.\n\n• It matters for roughly 1 million+ pages, or 10,000+ pages that change daily\n• Crawl budget = the set of URLs Google can and wants to crawl\n• Wasters: duplicate content, soft 404s, long redirect chains\n• noindex does not save budget: Google still requests the page, then drops it\n• Use robots.txt for pages you never want crawled\n• A 404 is a strong signal not to crawl a URL again\n• Keep your sitemap current\n\n#seo #technicalseo #crawlbudget #googlebot #seotips",
  "ig_caption": "Most sites do NOT have a crawl budget problem. 🕷️\n\n📏 Google: it matters at ~1M+ pages, or 10K+ that change daily\n🧮 Crawl budget = URLs Google can AND wants to crawl\n🗑️ Wasters: duplicates, soft 404s, long redirect chains\n⚠️ noindex does not save budget\n🚫 robots.txt stops the crawl\n🪦 404 = strong signal to stop\n\nFollow @indexfast for more.\n\nVoiceover is AI-generated. Source: Google Search Central.",
